# Exception: share project skills (SKILL.md only); rest of .claude/ stays ignored
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/*/
!.claude/skills/**/SKILL.md
# Exception: the PERMISSION RULES travel with the repository. They are the machine-neutral half —
# what an agent may run here without asking, and what must stop even at 3 a.m. Everything
# machine-specific (absolute paths, one-off allows) stays in settings.local.json, which is still
# ignored above. Before this, an unattended block's rules lived only on one disk.
!.claude/settings.json
client/coverage/
server/coverage/
client/playwright-report/
client/test-results/
.playwright-mcp/
/tmp/
AUDIT.md
audit-temp/
diagnosis/
# server/data is a pure runtime dir (gitignored). Shipped defaults live in server/seeds/
# and are copied here on boot. Keep only the README tracked.
server/data/**
!server/data/README.md
client/tmp/
# AUDIT-DOCS-1 (2026-09-04): `docs/diagnose/` no longer exists — the index was archived and
# diagnose reports live under `reports/`. Rule kept as a no-op would be a claim about a directory
# that is gone, so it is removed with the reason rather than left to puzzle the next reader.
# Root-level diagnostic screenshots and sweep artifacts (not part of the codebase)
/*.png
/sweep-*.txt
/sweep-*.mjs
# Sim raw data JSON files (too large for GitHub, reproduced via sim-fairness.mjs --seed=1)
reports/clean-state-2026-06-04/sim-phase2/fairness-data.json
docs/HANDOFF.md
# Sim/sweep raw output — reproduced on demand via scripts/sim-fairness.mjs; never committed.
results/
# Stray scratch stylesheet dump (leading-underscore; not imported anywhere).
client/_ul.css
# Night-run scaffolding. `logs/` is the unattended run's own output (docs/NIGHT-RUN.md owns the
# launcher that writes it) and `night-task.md` is the scratch brief handed to that run — neither is
# repository content, and the RUN'S FINDINGS live in reports/night/ which IS committed.
# WHY THEY ARE IGNORED RATHER THAN TOLERATED: the build stamp reads `git status --porcelain`, which
# counts untracked files, so leaving these two in the tree makes a bundle built from a clean commit
# report `+dirty` — at exactly the moment the owner is judging that bundle. A flag that cries wolf
# is worse than no flag.
logs/
night-task.md
